<item>
            <title>[LU-20660] ptlrpc: kick_cpu_latency() returns with latency_qos-&gt;lock held on allocation failure</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20660</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In lustre/ptlrpc/niobuf.c, kick_cpu_latency() takes latency_qos-&amp;gt;lock before allocating a struct dev_pm_qos_request. &#160;When OBD_ALLOC_PTR() fails, the function warns and returns immediately without dropping the mutex:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
  &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; mutex_lock(&amp;amp;latency_qos-&amp;gt;lock);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (latency_qos-&amp;gt;pm_qos_req == NULL) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; OBD_ALLOC_PTR(latency_qos-&amp;gt;pm_qos_req);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (latency_qos-&amp;gt;pm_qos_req == NULL) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; CWARN(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;%s: Failed to allocate a PM-QoS request &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; cpu %d\n&quot;&lt;/span&gt;,
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; obd-&amp;gt;obd_name, cpu);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; } &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
